1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:03,070
An owl can turn its head almost all the way around.

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:06,730
It has to, because its eyes aren't balls like ours.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,100
They're long tubes, locked in place,

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:10,610
so the head does the looking.

5
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:13,650
That twist would tear the blood vessels in your neck.

6
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:16,090
But an owl has fourteen neck bones,

7
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:17,430
twice as many as you.

8
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:21,410
Its arteries run through holes ten times wider than they are,

9
00:00:21,410 --> 00:00:23,910
cushioned with air, so they never get pinched.

10
00:00:24,210 --> 00:00:29,670
And under the jaw, they swell into little pools of blood that keep the brain fed while the head turns.

11
00:00:30,010 --> 00:00:32,220
So if one ever stares straight behind it,

12
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:33,333
don't panic, because
